// `caps(*)` hands `helper` the whole-resource wildcard of every domain that
// `main` holds, and as the entry module `main` holds all of them. It is the
// one-line delegation a program writes when it hands a library everything it
// may reach, instead of naming each domain: `impl "helper" caps(fs = ["/**"])`
// and its siblings say the same thing the long way.
impl "helper" caps(*)

fun main() {
    print(helper.read_two())
}
